---
import ArticleLayout from '../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { guide } from '../data/site';
---
<ArticleLayout title="Privacy" description="How this static website works, and what changes when you follow a link to the app, GitHub, or an external AI client." eyebrow="PROJECT / PRIVACY">
  <h2>This website</h2><p>The marketing website serves static pages and assets. This implementation has no accounts, email signup, hosted model storage, or AI chat service. It adds no analytics beacons, advertising pixels, fingerprinting, or session replay.</p><p>Fonts, images, and demonstration videos are served from the same site. The download selector keeps its current selections in page memory; it does not save them to cookies or browser storage. Copy buttons use the browser clipboard only after you activate them.</p>
  <h2>Hosting & operator</h2><p>This is a local review build. Production hosting, the responsible operator, contact details, and any hosting log-retention settings have not yet been configured. A production privacy notice must describe those actual arrangements before public launch.</p><p>A web host can process ordinary request information such as IP addresses and request headers. The absence of analytics scripts is not a claim that a hosting provider processes no data.</p>
  <h2>Downloads & external links</h2><p>SolidCore progress pages fetch public reports from bherbruck.github.io directly in your browser, without credentials or local storage. Failed requests show an error; no saved progress report is displayed. The homepage, download page, and release page request public release metadata from api.github.com. GitHub receives your IP address and ordinary request headers. No account token or credentials are sent. Validated public release metadata is cached in local browser storage for five minutes to reduce requests; the site still works when storage or GitHub is unavailable. Software downloads link directly to GitHub release assets. Documentation and browser buttons open the existing upstream project sites. Those services process requests under their own policies. This marketing website does not proxy downloads or add tracking parameters.</p>
  <h2>The browser application</h2><p>SolidCraft’s browser app is a separate application at a separate origin. Its saved documents and recovery behavior are described in the <a href={guide('files')}>file guide</a> and <a href={guide('updates')}>updates and privacy guide</a>. Keep exported backups of important designs.</p>
  <h2>AI clients & providers</h2><p>The website does not connect to your local MCP server or accept AI credentials. If you configure a compatible AI client separately, that client and its provider determine how prompts, tool results, screenshots, and other information are handled. Review their settings and policies.</p>
  <h2>Future changes</h2><p>Production deployment details must be reviewed before launch. Any later analytics, forms, storage, or hosted integrations require an updated description of what they do.</p>
</ArticleLayout>
